    { "", "A dungeon's story and the story of the place at its door are told once between them, not once outside and again inside.", "" },
    { "", "In a dungeon, a story a pull cuts off no longer starts over at every lull; it waits under Earlier for you to play it.", "" },
    { "\"Open What Willo keeps\" opens it", "ask Willo for the page, typed or out loud, and its button is in her window; before, she sometimes opened your Privacy settings instead while saying she had opened the page.", "\"Open What Willo keeps\" opens it:" },
    { "Community voices in other languages tell you what they need", "a community voice from /voices that can't play because its language pack isn't installed now says so in chat once, with where to get it, and Options shows it on the voice's row. Before, the English narrator read instead, with no word.", "Community voices in other languages tell you what they need:" },
    { "Read along shows what the voice says", "while a community voice reads a story from an older version of its text, Read along and the story's page in Found show the words you're hearing, then today's text once it stops.", "Read along shows what the voice says:" },
    { "Willo and add-ons", "asked for an add-on she doesn't know by name, she says so more often instead of offering one, and the ones she knows come with what they do and any catch.", "Willo and add-ons:" },
    { "", "Chinese: typing a story's older common name (第三次战争, 安度因·洛萨, 元素位面, 黑暗骑手) opens its story again.", "" },
    { "", "Willo misses fewer of your spoken questions: when her hearing is slow on one, she now tries again and answers instead of saying she didn't catch you.", "" },
    { "", "After you talk to a character in person, Willo no longer mixes their words into what you were doing.", "" },
    { "", "Ask Willo \"what did I do last time?\" in any chat, even a new one, and she tells you from your character's journey.", "" },
